'' AN EMBEDDED FILE IS A CACHE DEPENDENCY (docs/tiko-embed RFC-0001 §5.6): it goes into the
'' module's deps.txt like an included file, so rewriting it rebuilds the module that embeds
'' it, and the program sees the new bytes and the new bounds.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_MODCACHE=build/.mct-embed/cache
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.mct-embed
'' COPY: tests/modules/src/embedmod => build/.mct-embed
'' STEP: -v -target windows-x86_64 -i build/.mct-embed/libs build/.mct-embed/app/main.tiko -o build/.mct-embed/app.exe
'' WRITE: build/.mct-embed/libs/acme/res/logo.bin :: NEWLOGO!
'' ARGS: -v -target windows-x86_64 -i build/.mct-embed/libs build/.mct-embed/app/main.tiko -o build/.mct-embed/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.res: miss (a file it read changed)
'' RUN: build/.mct-embed/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: logo 7 N!
